air to begin with, but some sailors seek even greater thrills, such as hanging from a flying fin, or firing themselves from saltheap cannons.","abilities":["Movement Speed increases briefly when crossing a Rope Bridge or launched by a <Saltheap Cannon>"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.9,"stats":{"hp":5500,"atk":350,"def":50,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2}},"garum_gourmet":{"slug":"garum_gourmet","name":"Garum Gourmet","icon":"/enemies-icons/Garum Gourmet.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Sailors recommend their favorite things to each other, including saltfin garum. Some sailors take it a little too far, however, and roll their barrels into each other's faces.","abilities":["Movement Speed increases when carrying a Booze Barrel","First attack consumes Booze Barrel to deal heavy Physical damage and create an area where enemies gain increased ASPD and Physical Dodge"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.5,"stats":{"hp":9000,"atk":850,"def":500,"res":20,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":3}},"lucky_flyfin":{"slug":"lucky_flyfin","name":"Lucky Flyfin","icon":"/enemies-icons/Lucky Flyfin.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":null,"damageType":["No Damage"],"flavourText":"A female fin that leaps out of the salt layer during breeding season, gliding briefly in mid-air and releasing pleasant pheromones. Having one fall onto the deck is seen as a sign of good luck.","abilities":["Low-Altitude Hovering; after losing Low-Altitude Hovering, becomes stunned for some time before taking off again","Movement Speed briefly increases after taking damage for the first time. Sometimes carries <Risk-seeking Sailor>"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":10000,"atk":100,"def":0,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":1}},"bloody_chef":{"slug":"bloody_chef","name":"Bloody Chef","icon":"/enemies-icons/Bloody Chef.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"More butcher than cook, the fleet's chefs are more adept at dismembering carcasses than making the aftermath fit for human consumption. The smell of blood from the kitchen is enough to make even the most hardened sailors lose their appetite.","abilities":["More likely to be attacked","Nearby enemies and <Saltheap Cannons> take far less Physical/Arts damage from sources in the direction of the shield"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.5,"stats":{"hp":15000,"atk":1000,"def":1500,"res":40,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}},"anastasio_the_atoner":{"slug":"anastasio_the_atoner","name":"Anastasio, the Atoner","icon":"/enemies-icons/Anastasio, the Atoner.webp","rank":"Boss","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee and Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Anastasio has died. Anastasio rises again. He lives to atone for the sins ingrained in his very nature. He envies both the innocent for living and the sinner for dying, for it is not his place to either live with integrity or die in peace.","abilities":["Performs ranged attacks when unblocked, dealing Physical damage to the target and all allied units within the 8 surrounding tiles","[Gospel Spray] Fires within range 10 times, dealing Physical damage and Corrosion to the target and surrounding allied units, prioritizing allies with the lowest total Corrosion","First Form","Immune to the effects of Salt Flat, and takes far less Physical and Arts damage when in the surrounding 8 tiles around a <Saltheap Cannon>","[Inquisition of Sin] Buffs a <Saltheap Cannon> within Attack Range, increasing its splash area for a period of time","The first time HP drops to 0, jumps to a fixed spot and enters second form, summoning a <Saltheap Cannon>","Second Form","Immune to Stun; gains increased Movement Speed and ASPD","When another enemy appears, gains increased ATK, but loses HP per second for a period of time","When not blocked, takes significantly reduced Physical and Arts damage; when blocked, causes all <Saltheap Cannons> to target the location of the blocker","[Heart-Piercing Salvation] Whenever a certain amount of HP is lost, passes through the unit blocking him, dealing Physical damage to units along the path"],"levelCount":2,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":55000,"atk":1200,"def":500,"res":40,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}},"bridge_builder":{"slug":"bridge_builder","name":"Bridge Builder","icon":"/enemies-icons/Bridge Builder.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Portable and quick to build, rope bridges are a convenient way to connect two salt ships. Bridge builders are responsible for constructing them, but they still need others to help hold them in place and prevent them from falling apart.","abilities":["Invisible","Builds rope bridges that allow units to cross"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.65,"stats":{"hp":6000,"atk":600,"def":150,"res":30,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2}}},"dropIcons":{"4002":"/item-icons/originite_prime.png","30093":"/item-icons/grindstone.png","act39side_token_garum_rep_1":"/item-icons/saltfin_garum_act39side_token_garum_rep_1.png"},"previewFile":"ep-8.webp","emergency":null,"devices":[{"col":3,"description":"Less likely to get attacked by your units","hidden":false,"key":"trap_196_cnnon","kind":"device","name":"Saltheap Cannon","row":2},{"col":3,"description":"Less likely to get attacked by your units","hidden":false,"